their data platforms.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.030
Teams are shifting to dynamic
and AI-driven interactions.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.990
And it's not just about
data or more queries.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.020
The nature of the workload
itself is different.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.500
There's a shift towards
interactive experiences,

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.230
where users expect
immediate responses

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.480
and continuous iteration.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.850
Now, at the same time, scale

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.090
and concurrency are
increasing rapidly.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.080
These workloads are coming from
applications, agents, reports,

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.930
and pipelines, all
at the same time.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:25.740
And this is what's pushing data
warehousing to its limits.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.040
And as demand grows, traditional
scaling approaches begin

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.720
